@miley cyrus

They are broken apart so that the constructor could satisfy a feat of having a puzzle with full entries on every line. It would hardly have been possible to have a stack of 15 entries not broken up (even if they weren’t all 15 letters long, the black squares would be on the outside, so you’d need a bunch of 15 letter crossers in the middle. Quite impossible. As it is it’s a remarkable feat.

So it’s a little like Mt. Everest, the constructor did it to prove it could be done. You might not like the result, and many might agree with you; they might feel that they shouldn’t be subjected to the constructor’s vanity; and I sympathize with you on that, although I myself liked both the solve and seeing the artistry and challenge behind the puzzle’s conceit. But of course YMMV. In any case, I hope I’ve explained at least why they had to be split up.

